{#- One day of a learning cycle, with the reading itself inside it.

    Drawn as the front door is (design.md §12, 2026-09-27): the landing's bar, a hero
    with the cycle's manuscript beside the headline and the waitlist under it, today's
    reading, and the waitlist again at the foot.

    Nothing here is generated day to day. A calendar says which range, a cut takes it out
    of a text already on the shelf, and the page points at a reader built by a cron. -#}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ page_language|default('en') }}">
<head>
{% include '_public_head.html.j2' %}
<style>{{ asset('reader.css') }}{{ asset('public.css') }}{{ asset('front.css') }}</style>
{{ hebrew_face(true) }}
{{ chrome_face() }}
<script>{{ asset('keep.js') }}</script>
</head>
<body class="public front">
{#- The front door's bar (2026-09-27). -#}
{% with home = '/', here = ('/' ~ cycle.slug) if is_today else ('/' ~ cycle.slug ~ '/' ~ day.slug) %}{% include '_front_bar.html.j2' %}{% endwith %}
<main class="sheet weekly parasha daily">

  {#- The hero, as the front door draws it (2026-09-27): the headline and the waitlist on
      one side, the picture on the other as a card on the desk.

      The picture is a manuscript of the text the cycle reads — the Kaufmann Mishnah, the
      Aleppo Codex, the Leningrad Codex, the Gaza floor with David on it — and not a
      portrait of whoever is behind it. See `assets/manuscripts/README.md` and §12
      (2026-09-01): a page of the book is a picture of the book. -#}
  <section class="front-hero">
    <div class="headline">
      <p class="eyebrow">{% if is_today %}{{ t("daily.page.today", "Today") }}{% else %}{{ hdate(day.hdate) }}{% endif %}</p>
      <h1>{{ t("daily.page.pitch", "{name}, every word explained.", name=series(cycle.slug, "name")) }}</h1>
      <span class="named" lang="he" dir="rtl">{{ cycle.hebrew }}</span>
      <p class="lede">{{ series(cycle.slug, "what") }}</p>
      {#- The waitlist is for a stranger. Somebody who has chosen targum is not sold
          to again (§6), so for them the Read button leads the hero (copy audit,
          2026-09-28). -#}
      {%- if not signed_in %}
      {% with note = true %}{% include '_join_form.html.j2' %}{% endwith %}
      {%- endif %}
      <p class="actions">
        <a class="btn {{ 'cta' if signed_in else 'tonal' }}" href="#embed">{{ t("parasha.page.read", "Read") }} <bdi {% if day.hebrew %}lang="he" dir="rtl"{% else %}lang="en" dir="ltr"{% endif %}>{{ day.hebrew or day.title }}</bdi></a>
      </p>
      {%- if signed_in %}
      {%- with series_id = cycle.slug, says = t("subs.series.cycle-says", "Each day's instalment shows on Your targums and comes in your daily mail.") %}{% include '_series_subscribe.html.j2' %}{% endwith %}
      {%- endif %}
    </div>
    {#- Decoration: it says nothing the words have not said, so it is hidden from a
        screen reader rather than described to one. What it is and who wrote it is said
        in words further down, where a reader can read it. -#}
    <figure class="art" aria-hidden="true">
      <img src="{{ data_uri('manuscripts/' ~ cycle.picture) }}" alt="">
    </figure>
  </section>

  {#- What is read today, said twice: the way the cycle writes it and the way a Hebrew
      reader would. The Hebrew date under it, because that is the date this is keyed to
      and a page that only says "1 September" is a page about a Gregorian day. -#}
  <p class="dateline">
    <b {% if day.hebrew %}lang="he" dir="rtl"{% else %}lang="en" dir="ltr"{% endif %}><bdi>{{ day.hebrew or day.title }}</bdi></b>
    <span class="said-in-english">{{ ref(day.title) }}</span>
    <span class="when">{{ hdate(day.hdate) }}</span>
  </p>

  <div class="embed" id="embed">
    <button type="button" class="handle" id="embed-handle" aria-expanded="false">{{ t("daily.page.full-screen", "Full screen") }}</button>
    {#- The first section where there is more than one, and the whole thing where there
        is not — see `build.opens_at`. A day of Tehillim is seven psalms and its
        `index.html` is a list of seven links; a day of Mishna Yomi is one chapter and has
        no `sec-0001.html` to point at. -#}
    <iframe
      src="/{{ cycle.slug }}/read/{{ day.slug }}/reader/{{ opens }}"
      title="{{ ref(day.title) }}"
      loading="lazy"></iframe>
  </div>

  {#- The days either side, so somebody who missed yesterday can still read it and
      somebody looking ahead can. Only the ones actually built: the window rolls, and a
      link to a day that has fallen out of it is a link to a 404. -#}
  {% if nearby %}
  <nav class="nearby" aria-label="{{ t("daily.page.other-days", "Other days") }}">
    {%- for other in nearby %}
    <a class="day{% if other.day == day.day %} here{% endif %}"
       {% if other.day == day.day %}aria-current="page"{% endif %}
       href="/{{ cycle.slug }}/{{ other.slug }}">
      <span class="date">{{ hdate(other.hdate) }}</span>
      <bdi {% if other.hebrew %}lang="he" dir="rtl"{% else %}lang="en" dir="ltr"{% endif %}>{{ other.hebrew or other.title }}</bdi>
    </a>
    {%- endfor %}
  </nav>
  {% endif %}

  {#- The other cycles. Not a nav bar: four links, each saying what it reads today, which
      is the thing somebody deciding between them wants to know. -#}
  {% if others %}
  <section class="how">
    <h2 class="label">{{ t("daily.page.also-today", "Also today") }}</h2>
    <ol class="cycles">
      {%- for one, said in others %}
      <li>
        <b><a href="/{{ one.slug }}">{{ series(one.slug, "name") }}</a></b>
        <span>{{ t("daily.page.rhythm-today", "{rhythm} — today,", rhythm=series(one.slug, "rhythm")) }} <bdi lang="he" dir="rtl">{{ said }}</bdi></span>
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ol>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  <section class="honest">
    <h2 class="label">{{ t("daily.page.made-honestly", "Made honestly") }}</h2>
    {#- One key rather than four sentences with two blanks loose in the middle of them
        (targum-internal#348): who made the English and who took the picture are names,
        and everything around them is a sentence that a language puts in its own order. -#}
    <p class="made">
      {{ t("daily.page.made-honestly-says",
            "The Hebrew is the published edition, cut to this day's reading and not edited. The English beside it is {translation}. The cycle and its calendar come from Hebcal. The picture is {picture}.",
            translation=translation_said, picture=series(cycle.slug, "credit")) }}
    </p>
    {#- What Hebcal publishes and this shelf cannot read. A list, because it was a
        sentence with semicolons in it and the full stops inside each reason ran into
        them. Somebody looking for Daf Yomi is owed the reason, not a paragraph. -#}
    {% if absent %}
    <dl class="absent">
      {%- for name, why in absent %}
      <dt>{{ name }}</dt>
      <dd>{{ why }}</dd>
      {%- endfor %}
    </dl>
    {% endif %}
  </section>

  {#- The door is the waitlist (2026-09-27): a stranger who has read this far has no
      account to sign in to. The landing's own section, from the same file. -#}
  {%- if not signed_in %}
  {% include '_front_join.html.j2' %}
  {%- endif %}

</main>

{% if strings %}<script>window.TARGUM_STRINGS = {{ strings|tojson }};</script>
{% endif %}<script>{{ asset('strings.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('parasha.js') }}</script>

{% include '_public_foot.html.j2' %}
</body>
</html>
